import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — the weight-space lane: the conv+BN fold, derived or refused","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — the weight-space lane: the conv+BN fold, derived or refused","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/weightspace-fold.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/weightspace-fold.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/weightspace-fold.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t('<h1 id="retro-—-the-weight-space-lane-the-conv-bn-fold-derived-or-refused" tabindex="-1">Retro — the weight-space lane: the conv+BN fold, derived or refused <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-weight-space-lane-the-conv-bn-fold-derived-or-refused" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the weight-space lane: the conv+BN fold, derived or refused”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Tool</strong>: <code>lab/probes/weightspace_fold_probe.py</code> (merged <code>f83928d</code>). <strong>Depends on</strong>: plan 0025 (the missing law families), plan 0012 (bounded rewrites), ADR 0003.</p><h2 id="why-this-lane" tabindex="-1">Why this lane <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-this-lane" aria-label="Permalink to “Why this lane”">​</a></h2><p>The measured boundary from this cycle: models whose math is already fused expose nothing to the op-algebra laws (BiRefNet delivered FLOP-neutral). Three families were named as the expansion frontier; <strong>weight space</strong> is the one that tests the project&#39;s no-hardcoding rule — the fold must be <strong>derived</strong> by the machinery or <strong>refused</strong> with a named gap, never hand-written.</p><p>The fold is a pure identity on parameters:</p><pre><code>W&#39;[o] = W[o]·γ[o]/√(σ²[o] + ε)      b&#39; = (b − μ)·γ/√(σ² + ε) + β\n</code></pre><p>In IR terms it is a <strong>derived-leaf</strong> rewrite: the RHS weights are computed from the LHS&#39;s leaves. Real BiRefNet&#39;s decoder carries <strong>43 <code>nn.BatchNorm2d</code></strong> modules (<code>birefnet-bounded-lane.md</code>) and no conv+BN law ships.</p><h2 id="the-probe-s-gate-by-gate-account-measured" tabindex="-1">The probe&#39;s gate-by-gate account (measured) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-probe-s-gate-by-gate-account-measured" aria-label="Permalink to “The probe&#39;s gate-by-gate account (measured)”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>gate</th><th>verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>1 · binding source</strong></td><td>✅ the fold is a measured parameter identity — <code>Conv2d+BatchNorm2d</code> (eval): `max</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2 · <code>dspec_synth</code> fit</strong></td><td>⚠️ <strong>raw fold: no fit</strong> (<code>W&#39;</code> None, <code>b&#39;</code> None at depth 2–3). <strong>Pre-scaled: it fits</strong> — <code>W&#39; = mul(W, scale)</code>, and at depth 3 <code>b&#39; = add(beta, mul(scale, sub(b, mu)))</code>. So the fold&#39;s <em>structure</em> is derivable <strong>given a <code>scale</code> leaf</strong>; the missing piece is the derivation of <code>scale = γ/√(σ²+ε)</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>3 · cond DSL</strong></td><td>❌ <strong>no <code>sqrt</code>, no <code>rsqrt</code></strong>; float-exponent <code>pow</code> declines (<code>fdiv</code>/<code>recip</code> are fine) — so the DSL cannot spell <code>scale</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>4 · derive value domain</strong></td><td>❌ the derive value domain is **`int</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5 · e-graph visibility</strong></td><td>✅/❌ the IR <strong>does</strong> carry the node (<code>batch_norm</code> × 2 in the census), but <strong>no law LHS names it</strong> across 426 rules — nothing can rewrite it</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6 · cost model</strong></td><td>⚠️ <code>batch_norm</code> is <strong>absent from the FLOPs table</strong> (default price 256.0); <code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code> <em>are</em> present</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7 · derived-leaf seam</strong></td><td>✅ exists, is procedural, and registers source tensors</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="the-verdict-refused-with-the-gap-named-precisely" tabindex="-1">The verdict: refused, with the gap named precisely <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-verdict-refused-with-the-gap-named-precisely" aria-label="Permalink to “The verdict: refused, with the gap named precisely”">​</a></h2><p>The fold is <strong>structurally derivable</strong> — the synthesizer finds the correct two-expression form once a <code>scale</code> leaf is supplied, which is strong evidence the machinery understands the rewrite&#39;s shape. It <strong>cannot be completed</strong> for two independent, measured reasons:</p><ol><li><strong>The cond/derive DSL has no square root</strong> (<code>sqrt</code>/<code>rsqrt</code> absent; float <code>pow</code> declines) — <code>scale = γ/√(σ²+ε)</code> is unspellable.</li><li><strong>The derive value domain is scalar</strong> (<code>int | float</code>) — a per-channel tensor <code>scale</code> cannot be computed as a derived value, even if the DSL gained an <code>rsqrt</code>.</li></ol><p>Plus two gaps that are <em>content</em>, not capability, and are therefore the parts a human may legitimately author:</p><ol start="3"><li><strong>No law LHS names <code>batch_norm</code></strong> — the rewrite does not exist in the library (this is what the derived law would <em>be</em>).</li><li><strong><code>batch_norm</code> is unpriced</strong> in the FLOPs table, so the fold would not be ranked even if it existed.</li></ol><h2 id="what-this-buys-the-project" tabindex="-1">What this buys the project <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-buys-the-project" aria-label="Permalink to “What this buys the project”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>The no-hardcoding principle held under test</strong>: the machine derived the fold&#39;s <em>structure</em> and refused the rest with named causes — rather than a human writing <code>conv_bn_fold</code> and calling it done.</li><li><strong>A concrete, ordered backlog</strong>: (a) tensor-valued derive leaves (the <code>source_tensors</code> seam exists but the value domain does not admit them), (b) <code>rsqrt</code>/<code>sqrt</code> in the derive DSL, (c) <code>batch_norm</code> in the FLOPs table, (d) the law itself — derivable once (a)+(b) land.</li><li><strong>An OOM class found and fixed</strong>: the probe&#39;s depth-3 <code>dspec_synth</code> sweep over the fold&#39;s seven-attr bank is <strong>quartic in leaf count</strong> and OOM-killed the process (measured: <code>MemoryError</code> under a 4 GB cap after ~17 s; an OS OOM-kill without one). Routing every fit through <code>dspec_audit.bounded_synth</code> (same candidate space, deepest level streamed with early bail under a wall-clock budget) makes it run end to end — the same class of unbounded-sweep risk the discovery work has hit before.</li></ul><h2 id="honest-limits" tabindex="-1">Honest limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#honest-limits" aria-label="Permalink to “Honest limits”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Measured on CPU, small shapes (<code>W(6,4,3,3)</code>, <code>W(6,8)</code>), fp64 — the identity is what is being verified, not a speedup.</li><li>The probe <em>refuses</em> rather than <em>derives</em>: this retro records a negative, and the negative is the result.</li><li>No pay was measured, because nothing could be admitted — the two blockers above come first.</li></ul>',18)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};